WEBVTT

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.660
Kana-san and Morishita-san are spies?!

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.420
Shocking, isn't it?

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.780
We use spies to provide a safe environment at this school.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:17.160
The amount of money that moves through this school can reach tens of billions of yen each year.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.040
While student autonomy holds the foreground in their talks,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.170
in the background, the old boys are holding power struggles of their own.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:29.840
<i>She</i> was caught up in some of this intrigue.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.680
In December of last year, she was in an accident.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.620
We believe that she was targeted while investigating something.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:43.840
The camera's memory card, which we believe held evidence of the intrigue,

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.040
had been removed.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.900
And Kana-san's been in a coma ever since?

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.980
In order to keep the existence of S-agents confidential,

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.830
news of her accident has been kept under wraps.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.020
She is currently receiving treatment at a hospital

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.820
run by a former member of the Public Safety Commission.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.240
The hospital is renowned for its treatment concerning cases like hers,

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.240
so everything has gone well so far.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.840
However, we have another problem on our hands.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.900
Yeah. That's what it looks like.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.980
The President insists on putting Oojima Yuuki on the throne.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.980
Could you help me out a little?

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.000
Chisato?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.060
I'm coming in.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.040
Chisato...

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:18.200
Did something happen?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.700
No.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.280
Nothing?

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.420
The election is right around the corner, you know.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.410
I don't care about the election.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:29.080
But if we lose, the Food Club will be disbanded!

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.600
I don't care about the Food Club.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.350
I don't care.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.500
Chisato...

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.700
That hospital is affiliated with the Katahira Faction.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.200
Katahira Faction?

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.600
Internal strife.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.840
They're our rivals within the Commission.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.840
One of the conditions for admitting her into the hospital

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:53.750
was appointing Oosawa Yuina as Public Safety Commissioner.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:58.630
How... How can you use that to decide who to appoint to such an important role?!

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.170
So you're saying I should have just watched as she died?

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.040
No, what I meant was...

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:07.370
I'm sure you'd be able to do it.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:10.620
The same way you heartlessly refused to eat her chocolate.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.100
H-How do you know about that?!

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:17.140
After losing her brother, Sumiyoshi-san has been depending on you for support all her life.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.420
But you threw her aside.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.500
What do you mean?!

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:26.820
Didn't you swear to play Daiki-kun's replacement for her forever?

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.940
This is what went through your head.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.260
If, one day, Sumiyoshi-san came to terms with Daiki-kun's death,

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:37.220
you would no longer be of use to her.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.320
Don't act like you know—

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.380
Am I wrong?

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.760
You used Daiki-kun as an excuse to hide from your own feelings.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.050
You even stopped believing anything she said.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:50.460
But even when you tried to fall in love with another girl,

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.100
she was always in the back of your mind.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.340
You couldn't commit.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:55.540
Hmph.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.260
It's actually pretty funny.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.120
What'd you say?!

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:04.780
I wish it were all that simple for me.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:09.200
For me, who might lose someone I love...

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.880
You got into a fight with Yuu-kun, huh?

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.330
How did you know?

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.360
You <i>are</i> my best friend.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.590
Why don't we talk things over with him?

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:24.860
Come on, let's go.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.240
Leave me alone!

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.180
Don't be like that. You need to talk things through.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.510
Leave me alone!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:34.860
If you don't make up, things will only get worse.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.020
Let's get you changed first.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.270
No! Don't open that!

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:46.880
Chocolate?

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.760
But you don't eat chocolate...

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.620
What happened to the missing halves?

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.340
Yuuki.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.420
You've been using him as a replacement for your brother?

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.040
No!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.260
No...

00:05:58.260 --> 00:05:59.660
I haven't...

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:04.560
Chisato, aren't you in love with Yuu-kun?

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:08.400
You need to see him for who he is.

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:12.520
You can't treat him as a replacement for Daiki-kun forever—

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:13.560
Leave me alone!

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.730
Why don't you worry about yourself instead of me, Mifuyu?!

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:20.020
You're in love with Yuuki, too, right?

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.940
You thought I didn't know?

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:23.500
What are you—

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.500
Are you holding back for my sake?

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:28.540
Or is it the scar from your surgery?

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:33.450
It's fine. Yuuki wouldn't mind something like that.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:36.120
Don't hold back on my account.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:36.880
Stop.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.660
Why don't you just ask him out?

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:39.320
Stop.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:41.420
I think Yuuki's into you just as much.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.380
Stop!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.590
I know he'll say yes!

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:45.620
Stop!

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:50.470
Please, don't say any more.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:56.180
We will soon lose our position as ruling party.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:00.640
When a new party comes to power, they will audit our spending.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.140
Without a doubt,

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:05.940
it will be exposed that Public Safety funds were used to pay for her treatment.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:10.280
Once that happens, we will be unable to continue her treatment.

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:15.640
I was at the gates of Hell itself when I met you.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.380
If you were elected President...

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:21.080
If you could see things my way...

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.830
If you could, then Kana would...

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:28.400
You've far exceeded my expectations.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.260
You're caught in a dead heat for first place now.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.680
But the situation has changed.

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:38.680
I've just received word from the head of the Katahira Faction...

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:42.760
to cease all support for Oojima Yuuki.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:45.140
If I don't, they'll cease all treatment for Kana.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:54.260
I wanted to be forgiven.

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:59.780
I wanted someone to forgive me.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:07.210
Daiki couldn't even eat his favorite chocolate before he died because I was mean that day.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.260
Now he's gone.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:14.280
He isn't around to forgive me.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.320
Yuuki ate my chocolate.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.200
Just watching him eat it saved my soul.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.860
I was really happy.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.920
I love Yuuki.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.450
So much.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:32.820
But I can't let myself be happy, no matter what!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.360
Daiki can never be happy again!

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:37.240
Chisato...

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.540
Mifuyu?

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:50.340
When I was held back a year and felt out of place in my own class,

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:54.050
you talked to me without minding it in the least.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.420
When I felt alone and abandoned...

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.560
When I was suffering and needed help...

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.700
You reached out to me.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.060
You saved me.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:09.570
So it hurts me to see you suffering.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.650
Mifuyu...

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.160
How do I look?

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:18.700
Stop...

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:21.970
I can't let you bear this pain alone.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:22.780
So...

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.290
Mifuyu!

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:35.720
Mifuyu!

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:45.230
<i>I... I can't stay bound by the past.</i>

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:48.600
<i>I'm a year older than them.</i>

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.140
<i>If I'm too scared...</i>

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:53.760
<i>I have to keep moving forward.</i>

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.280
<i>This...</i>

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.640
<i>is nothing.</i>

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.940
I'm sorry.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.260
I'm so sorry!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.460
Chisato...

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:18.090
No more... Just stop...

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:27.020
I know you love Daiki-kun very much.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:32.940
But do you think Daiki-kun wants you to suffer because of that?

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:36.910
Daiki can never be happy again.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:39.160
I can't go off and be happy by myself.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.320
I'm sure Daiki-kun is happy.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.330
After all, you love him so much.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.060
Mifuyu!

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.700
That's all I can tell you.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.340
Do you understand?

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:04.600
Did you tell Morishita-san about Kana-san?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:05.980
I have not.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:06.970
Why not?!

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:12.220
Kana's situation is confidential information that few know, even in the Public Safety Commission.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:13.420
But...

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:16.230
I will hold you to that same confidentiality.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.380
I told you that there was no going back once you heard it.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:25.620
If you tell anyone, I will use the Public Safety Commission to bring you down.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.580
Our partnership ends here.

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:33.260
I thought you could put up a good fight, too.

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:34.400
It's unfortunate.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:40.820
I'm sorry I put you through all this.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.680
You've exerted so much fruitless time and effort.

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:47.740
I'll make arrangements for the Food Club not to be disbanded.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:51.850
That way, our partnership won't have been for naught.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.400
Do you understand?

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.840
I understand.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:00.780
But you've got a few things wrong.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:01.990
First,

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.100
it wasn't fruitless.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.120
Second,

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.790
we don't need your partnership anymore.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.210
Because...

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:14.630
I have every intention of being elected.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.130
And finally, I have one last thing to say.

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.340
Get his phone!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:29.560
Oojima?

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.880
Morishita-san!

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.520
Kana-san is in Hatsushiba General Hospital! Hurry!

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.060
What's the meaning of this?

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:43.950
I won't let you get your way.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.220
You never consulted anyone about anything!

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:49.410
Not about the election, and not about Morishita-san!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:53.660
Did you want her to search for Kana-san forever?

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:58.750
It seems you <i>didn't</i> understand, Stupidjima-kun.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:01.130
Depending on what happens next,

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.920
I may need to dispose of you.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:10.380
Headquarters to all personnel.
An intruder is in the building.

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.230
Security level raised to maximum.

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:12.810
Roger.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:18.440
Excuse me!

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:21.960
Where are you going?

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:23.690
To give a shot.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.640
At this hour?

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:27.320
Excuse me, but I need you to come—

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.780
Kana!

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:49.820
Find Morishita Michiru immediately.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:50.890
Yes, sir!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.140
It's me. This is urgent.

00:13:57.710 --> 00:13:59.130
Kana...

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:01.400
If anything happens to Kana,

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.730
I will have your head!

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:13.910
I wanted to see you.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.920
I was so lonely without you.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.920
Your harmonica broke, too.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:23.900
I looked everywhere for you.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:27.050
I thought I could find you if I became an S-agent,

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.430
so I came to Takafuji.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:37.780
I practiced that song you taught me.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.160
You're... pretty good now.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:47.480
Kana-chan?

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:50.360
Kana-chan!

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:02.440
The clouds cast orange by the setting sun
ano yuuhi ni somaru kaze

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:07.320
The laughter we heard coming from the grounds
guraundo kara hibiku waraigoe

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:11.720
The sunlight that we saw after school
houkago no hikari ga

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:16.450
Filtering into the hallways
furisosogu watari rouka

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:20.220
The sky that we now still can't reach
mada todokanai ano sora

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:25.080
Together, we always watched it go by
issho ni miageteita

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:29.880
I'll never forget seeing you by my side
kimi no yokogaohitomi wo

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:33.580
And seeing your eyes looking up
zutto wasurenai yo

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:38.510
In the classroom, with no one else but us,
dare mo inai kyoushitsu de futari

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:45.720
We would tell each other about all the dreams we had
ikusenmono yume wo katariatta ne

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:49.650
Before I knew it, you were always there
ki ga tsukeba kimi ga itsumo

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:54.450
And always giving me reasons to smile
watashi ni egao kuretan da

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:59.060
Whenever we grow closer together,
kokoro chikadzuku tabi ni

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:03.080
I can feel my heart beating faster
takanaru kodou kanjiteta

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:08.110
I hope you'll always be there smiling,
douka waratteite kitto

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:12.630
Just like the way that you do now
ari no mama no kimi de

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:20.770
For giving me this shining, bright, and brilliant season I want to tell you,
tobikiri sukitooru kagayaku kisetsu wo kureta kimi ni

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:24.270
Thank you so much
arigatou

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:55.260
I thought Yakumo-senpai stopped supporting him.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.300
That's correct. Our sources can confirm this.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.500
Then what's with these numbers?

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.310
I believe he earned them on his own merit.

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:03.060
Election Special
I believe he earned them on his own merit.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.560
Election Special

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.280
What would you like to do?

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.980
Could you call in S-chan?

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:09.980
Right away.

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:13.220
And I'll need to pay a little visit.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.740
Good work, everyone!

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:20.480
The debate was a huge success!

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:21.340
You think so?

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:23.990
You were at the top of the polls for a moment!

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:26.900
Ooshima getting elected might be more than just a dream!

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:29.340
We might win! We might actually <i>win</i>!

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:31.640
All right! Tomorrow's the big day!

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:35.130
We're hitting 'em with one last speech before they start punching those ballots!

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.760
Let's do our best, Oojima-senpai!

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.120
I think I might have a heart attack.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.470
Wow, maybe you're not cut out to be a presidential candidate.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:45.850
Oh, right. There's a good way of dealing with that.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.840
Right, Ms. Campaign Manager?

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:54.300
So why do I have to go on a date with you?

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:54.900
Beats me.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.360
Ask Mifuyu.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:19:00.220
Did something happen between the two of you?

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.370
You could say that.

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:06.120
What?! You can't make it?!

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:08.500
Don't do this to me, man.

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:10.840
Preparations for the ceremony are already—

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:11.860
Wait!

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:18.060
Excuse me, you two!

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:22.970
Excuse me, but would you two happen to be a couple?

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:24.970
Yes, we are!

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.180
What?! A coup—

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:28.060
That's perfect!

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:32.190
I know this is sudden, but could you two do me a favor?

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:34.100
Please! I'm begging you!

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:38.720
And now, here comes the bride!

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:03.840
Don't need to do it for real.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.220
Congratulations on your marriage!

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:13.230
Thank you!

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.860
<i>Congratulations on your marriage!</i>

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:24.740
<i>They're beautiful! Thank you.</i>

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.450
<i>You'll be the one coming to our wedding next!</i>

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:30.410
<i>I see you two are in love.</i>

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.120
<i>"Love"?</i>

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:38.600
<i>Back then, I didn't know what love was.</i>

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:40.560
<i>And I still...</i>

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:44.400
Reminds me of when we were little.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:47.440
We did this before when we were kids.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:48.690
Yeah.

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:50.430
<i>Wait. I remember now.</i>

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:55.000
<i>Back then, I was already in love with Chisato.</i>

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.340
<i>It wasn't that I didn't know what it was.</i>

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:59.420
<i>I just never realized that I was in it.</i>

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.300
That dinner was amazing!

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:09.370
The steak in that main course practically melted in my mouth!

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:11.260
I'd love to eat it again.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:12.120
Yeah.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:14.620
Together.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:23.820
What's up?

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:26.160
People were watching back there.

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:26.800
Huh?

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.720
No one's watching us now.

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:52.540
Yuuki?!

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:23.570
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:27.530
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:31.670
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:35.750
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:40.090
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:44.250
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:48.280
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:54.760
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:56.390 --> 00:23:01.400
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:05.570
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:07.760
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:11.460
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:13.990
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:18.250
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:22.130
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:27.890
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:35.760
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:42.250 --> 00:23:45.570
Different people like different kinds of sweets.

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:49.080
According to a recent poll, 50% of people surveyed like Western sweets,

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:51.640
and the other 50% like Japanese sweets.

00:23:51.640 --> 00:23:53.400
My, it's split very evenly.

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:56.860
50% of people surveyed are worried about their diets when they eat sweets,

00:23:56.860 --> 00:23:59.020
and the other 50% have given up and just eat them.

00:23:59.020 --> 00:24:00.460
That one's split evenly, too.

00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:04.040
And 100% of people regret eating them after the fact.

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:05.080
Everyone does?

00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:07.020
Next time, Episode 12: "Election Day!"

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:08.960
How many people were in that poll?

00:24:08.960 --> 00:24:10.200
Two people, just now.
